comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T07:57:37.866Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for Sentry 10.69 and Greptile 3.3 found only prior closed refresh lineages and broader quality parents; this date-specific compatible refresh is new work. npm-package-arg 14 remains canonically tracked by pm-ksr40d and TypeScript 7 by pm-do5b."
  "2026-07-31T08:18:38.723Z","harness:codex","Packed consumer proof: an unrelated fresh npm project installed the repository tarball plus TypeScript 6 and Node declarations, compiled a strict NodeNext SDK import with no emit, and resolved the packaged pm executable. This proves Sentry 10.69 declaration compatibility after the known 10.68 regression."
  "2026-07-31T08:29:31.910Z","harness:codex","Sentry/release-gate evidence: PM-CLI-2T (event 90400f0e8ae34b7f9c86440a19005757) is a single handled write failure at 2026-07-31T07:42:37Z from the current v2026.7.31 checkout. Host diagnostics showed /tmp at 89% inode utilization during the earlier acceptance/release-gate run. The packed consumer and full 6,585-test coverage suite subsequently passed with home-backed temporary storage. This is a bounded runner resource-exhaustion incident, not a product or dependency regression; resolve the isolated event and re-run the live Sentry/telemetry release gate."
  "2026-07-31T08:31:36.136Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: @sentry/node 10.69 and Greptile 3.3 passed clean audit, packed strict NodeNext consumer compilation, executable containment, 407-file/6,585-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, and the live Sentry/telemetry gate with 0 blocking issues."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T08:31:36.898Z","harness:codex","Dependency compatibility must be proven from a packed unrelated TypeScript consumer, not only the repository build. Transient package-manager write failures under tmpfs inode pressure should be separated from declaration regressions with home-backed acceptance."
